{
 "_about": "Matt's flagged faults (25 Oct) as the calibration set for both gates. The screenshots are Matt's and stay local (never committed): pass their folder with --flagged. Boxes are in art px of each picture after core.to_native (the woodland shot is 3066 x 1740 at 3.14 screen px a texel, Retina; the crops likewise; 49583f7d is 6.28). Each fault lists what must catch it: 'screen' = the scene gate's image detectors on Matt's picture, 'zone' = the scene gate's data checks on the Godot zone, 'asset' = the asset gate on the asset that draws it. A fault counts as caught when at least one listed route finds it with a listed detector (in the box, for screen and zone routes). Asset refs are pinned to the commit Matt saw ('zone/name@commit', 'file:<repo path>@commit|x0,y0,x1,y1' for a frame of a sheet), so later redraws do not change the calibration. Kit pieces are drawn from the generator, so the two Matt saw (W6, W10) are kept as rendered at main 561235c2 under scripts/review/calibration/kit/ (pinned 26 Oct, fix queue 2). W15 is not Matt's: the plunge pool's foam an independent detail-auditor failed on 4 Nov (docs/reviews/2026-11-04-woodland-water.md), frozen from 4881fee7 as scripts/review/calibration/woodland_plunge_foam_4881fee7.png (ground.png 140..420 x 740..960), so the foam check never loses it. F1 to F13 (12 Nov) are Matt's Frostline misses that an independent detail-auditor had passed: his screenshots frost_hut_stream.png, frost_fall_step.png and frost_stair.png (local only; their scales are pinned in 'images' because they are smoothed zooms core.to_native cannot measure), the art pinned to #478's round 3 head bf525d25, and the further misses of rounds 4 and 5 pinned to 0b122ffe and 0ef53b94 (F11, F12, F13). 'kitplan' = kit_overlap on a kit zone's plan at a commit. A fault with 'open' has no detector yet: the reason says what was measured; the auditors judge it by eye (docs/review-agents.md, Matt's 12 Nov misses) and it does not count in the recall gate.",
